ctively. Soil texture, climate zone and crop type were also found significant factors to increase GHGs emissions. Thus, this meta-analysis revealed a knowledge gap concerning the consequences of animal manure application and rate, climate zone, and physicochemical properties of soil on GHGs emissions from agricultural soils. © 2020 Elsevier Ltd\n\nReview Question: What is the impact of animal manure application to agricultural soils on greenhouse gas emissions\n######################\nOutput:'}
