med by using mixed model methodology in which different studies were treated as random effects whereas 3-NOP addition levels in diets of ruminants were treated as fixed effects. Results showed that increasing level of 3-NOP addition in diets of ruminants decreased enteric CH4 emissions per unit of body weight, CH4/DMI, CH4/milk produced, CH4/digested organic matter or CH4/gross energy intake (p<.05). Production of H-2 was higher with increasing level of 3-NOP addition (p<.001). Addition of 3-NOP decreased total VFA concentration (p<.01), and decreased and increased proportions of C-2 and C\n######################\nOutput:'}
