forestry significantly increased SOC stock of 26, 40, and 34% at 0-15, 0-30, and 0-100 cm respectively. The conversion from pasture/grassland to agroforestry produced significant SOC stock increases at 0-30 cm (9%) and 0-30 cm (10%). Switching from uncultivated/other land-uses to agroforestry increased SOC by 25% at 0-30 cm, while a decrease was observed at 0-60 cm (23%). Among agroforestry systems, significant SOC stocks increases were reported at various soil horizons and depths\n######################\nOutput:'}
