trate N (NO3 (-)), microbial biomass C (MBC) and N (MBN), rates of nitrification (NTF) and denitrification (DNF), as well as C/N ratio. The results depicted that all these variables showed significant changes (P < 0.05) with [O-3] increased by 27.6 +/- 18.7 nl l(-1) (mean +/- SD), including decreases in TC, DOC, TN, NH4 (+), MBC, MBN and NTF, and increases in C/N, NO3 (-) and DNF. The effect sizes of TN, NTF, and DNF were significantly correlated with O-3 fumigation levels and experimental duration (P < 0.05).\n######################\nOutput:'}
