scaled N2O emissions (N2O intensity) from croplands to deep fertilization, and (ii) identify the soil, climate, and management factors that mitigate N2O emissions and N2O intensity under deep fertilization. RESULTS: Compared with the control, deep fertilization increased N2O emissions by 18.6% (P &lt; 0.001) but decreased N2O intensity by 20.1% (P = 0.018). By adopting deep fertilization, N2O emissions could be significantly mitigated in rice-paddies soils (\u221248.8%), with fertilizer depth &gt; 10 cm (\u221233.0%), and with fertilizer N amount &gt; 200 kg N ha\u22121 (\u22128.2%). N2\n######################\nOutput:'}
