h 234 observations from 89 individual studies and analysed the role of experimental method, soil properties, fertilizer/NI type, fertilizer application rate and land use type as explanatory factors. Furthermore, using data sets where soil NH3 emission and N2O emission were measured simultaneously, we re-evaluated the effect of NI on overall N2O emissions including indirect N2O emission from NH3 volatilization. We found that, on average, NIs increased NH3 volatilization by 35.7% (95% CI: 25.7–46.7%) and increased indirect N2O emission from NH3 emission (and subsequent N deposition) by 2.9%–15.2%. Responses of NH3 volatilization mainly varied with experimental method\n######################\nOutput:'}
