 34.62, 19.48, and 62.16%, respectively. The effect size of moderate grazing was significantly lower than that of high grazing (p < 0.05). The effect size of grazing on pH was significant (p < 0.05), and pH increased by 6.51% compared with control. Both soil ammonia and nitrate levels increased by 12.24 and 8.60%, respectively. However, grazing decreased soil total carbon, total phosphorus, and available phosphorus by 14.4, 10.25, and 10.15%, respectively. Grazing significantly decreased plant diversity (p < 0.05), richness, and aboveground biomass\n######################\nOutput:'}
